  "notes": "Sasini Plc \u2014 Kenyan agribusiness listed on the Nairobi Securities Exchange (NSE Kenya). Owns ~32,000 ha (~79k acres) of tea, coffee, macadamia and avocado estates in Kericho, Kiambu and Nandi counties + dairy operations. Diversification away from pure tea over past decade has dampened earnings volatility. Fiscal year ends 30 September. KES reporting; figures in KES millions. Tea price downturn FY2023-2024 hit profitability (sector-wide pressure on Kenyan tea auction prices), partly offset by macadamia/avocado growth. Net debt rose modestly post-FY2022 driven by working-capital and replanting capex. Acres ~79k (32k ha including newer macadamia/avocado expansion). Pre-2022 figures show stronger margins on tea-led mix.",
